This project is deliberately split across two licences, along the line of what links
the engine. See DESIGN.md § 13.

  AGPL-3.0-or-later  (LICENSE)
    packages/core     the continuity engine
    packages/daemon   file watcher and tier orchestration
    packages/lsp      language server
    packages/mcp      MCP server

    These embed the engine, so the combined work carries its licence. The intent is to
    prevent a closed SaaS strip-mine of the core.

  Apache-2.0         (LICENSE-APACHE)
    packages/spec     the on-disk bible format, the wire protocol, and the JSON-RPC
                      transport
    clients/vscode    VS Code extension
    clients/obsidian  Obsidian plugin

    These speak the protocol without linking the engine — the clients launch
    prosebind-lsp as a separate process. The format and protocol are meant to be
    adopted, re-implemented and embedded freely, including commercially. An adopted
    format outlives any one implementation of it.

Third-party dependencies retain their own licences. At the time of writing the only
runtime dependency of the engine is `yaml` (ISC).
